The commercial aircraft battery market plays an important role in aviation safety and operational reliability. Aircraft batteries provide power for engine starting, auxiliary power units (APUs), onboard electrical systems, and emergency functions. Fleet expansion, aircraft modernization, and the gradual adoption of advanced battery technologies are shaping demand across the aviation industry.

What Is the Commercial Aircraft Battery Market?
The commercial aircraft battery market covers battery systems designed for commercial aviation applications. These batteries supply electrical power during ground operations, support auxiliary systems, regulate DC network voltage, and provide backup power during electrical failures. Nickel-based batteries remain established in many aircraft platforms, while lithium-based technologies are attracting interest because of their higher energy density and lower weight.

