Key Market Drivers
Expansion of Global Aircraft Fleets and MRO Activities
Growing air passenger traffic is encouraging airlines to expand and modernize their fleets. Each commercial aircraft requires reliable battery systems for engine starting, auxiliary power, and emergency backup. Fleet expansion therefore supports demand for original equipment batteries, while aircraft maintenance, repair, and overhaul activities generate recurring replacement demand.

Transition Toward More Electric Aircraft
The aviation industry's shift toward more electric aircraft architectures is increasing the importance of onboard electrical systems. Greater electrical loads require batteries with improved energy density, power output, and reliability. This transition is encouraging manufacturers to develop advanced battery technologies suited to modern aircraft platforms.

Demand for Lightweight and Fuel-Efficient Aircraft
Airlines and aircraft manufacturers are seeking ways to reduce aircraft weight and improve fuel efficiency. Lithium-ion batteries offer weight advantages over traditional battery chemistries and are gaining attention for selected aviation applications. Continued improvements in battery safety and certification are supporting this technology transition.

